request.description:
Returns all configured search locations. Call this first to discover which indexes are available, then reference them in the `location` field of search requests.

**Response:**
```json
{
  "locations": [
    {
      "name": "myproject",
      "folders": ["C:/src/myproject"],
      "extensions": [".py", ".js"],
      "indexMode": "filenameAndContent"
    }
  ]
}
```

`indexMode` is one of `filenameAndContent`, `content`, or `filename`.

Search file names. Supports `*` and `?` wildcards. Matches against the file name only (not the full path). When the query contains a `.`, the part after the last `.` is treated as an extension filter (e.g. `*.py`).

**Response:**
```json
{
  "totalFiles": 5000,
  "files": [
    "C:/src/myproject/src/Factory.py"
  ]
}
```
